Page No. 2 of 21 respondent no. 1 and 2, wherein it is stated inter alia that the answering respondents have been wrongly impleaded by the petitioner in collusion with the police; that the petitioner's friend himself was driving the car in a rash and negligent manner; that the accident was not caused due to any rash or negligent driving on the part of respondent no. 1, who had been involved by the petitioner later on, in order to get compensation;
that respondent no. 1 was having valid driving license and the said vehicle was fully insured with respondent no. 3, who is liable to indemnify the claim of the petitioner, in case Court comes to the conclusion that accident was caused by the respondent no. 1.
4.

In his cross-examination done by the Ld. Counsel for the respondent no.3, PW-1 stated inter alia that he was returning from shopping at 11 pm on the date of accident;
that his vehicle was hit with Trola from backside which was of big size with 16 tyres;
that he saw the Trola just before the accident; that his vehicle was being driven in the center of the road; that Trola was going ahead of him and accident took place as side of Trola hit his vehicle while it was trying to negotiate U turn.
